; fas9_order_index.scr - facit for step 9.4 (draw order, clipping and indexes; F9.4). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_order_index.scr
; (AutoCAD 2025's core, a new empty drawing from acad.dwt). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP; see fas9_example.scr.
;
; What it draws: layers HDXF_A and HDXF_B; a block HDXF_INDEXED with a line on one and a circle on the other layer;
; three INSERTs of it, each with its own XCLIP (a rectangle, a polygon with front and back clip planes, an inverted
; rectangle); model space entities with DRAWORDER (SORTENTSTABLE of the model space) and two entities in Layout1 with
; DRAWORDER (the paper space's). INDEXCTL 3 with a native DWG save makes AutoCAD itself build the LAYER_INDEX with its
; IDBUFFERs and the SPATIAL_INDEX; the DXF saves that follow carry them. Then one change per pair: a layer change, an
; erased indexed entity, a changed draw order, a deleted clip boundary.
;
; (The core has no screen: ZOOM E gives a view in which points can be picked.)
;
; Not made here (the core has no command for them; see plan 9.4, "Ej testat"): a LAYER_FILTER (AutoCAD's own is in
; doc/facit/acad_*_dxf_native_records.dxf, made by 21_native_records.scr in the GUI), a SPATIAL_FILTER in an xref
; (needs an xref drawing), an IDBUFFER of a user (not an index).
